A steel tube is rigidly fastened between aluminum and bronze rods and the axial loads are applied at the position shown. Find the maximum value of $P$ that will not exceed stress of $80$ MPa in aluminium, $100$ MPa in bronze and $150$ MPa in steel, given the following details:

Aluminium: $A = 200\ \text{mm}^2$, $L = 1\ \text{m}$;

Steel: $A = 400\ \text{mm}^2$, $L = 2\ \text{m}$;

Bronze: $A = 500\ \text{mm}^2$, $L = 3\ \text{m}$.

